---
/**
 * /samdrea/dj — RETIRED. Redirects to the page that replaced it.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHAT WAS HERE, AND WHY IT IS NOT ANY MORE
 *
 * This was "the booth": a passcode-gated page where Sam posted his half of the
 * song of the day, plus a feed of her reactions. It existed because the wing
 * started ONE-DIRECTIONAL — he posted, she read — and when it went mutual her half
 * moved onto /samdrea/vault/today while his never followed. So the feature called
 * "one day, two songs" was split across two pages and needed two logins.
 *
 * Both halves of it are now redundant:
 *
 *   THE POSTING FORM lives on /samdrea/vault/today, next to hers, gated on the
 *   viewer so each of them sees only their own. /api/us/song accepts a session like
 *   every other write in the wing and reads `who` from the cookie.
 *
 *   THE REACTIONS FEED was already on that page — they render inside his card, on
 *   the song they belong to, which is a better place for them than a separate list.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * AND THE PASSCODE WAS NEVER BUYING WHAT IT LOOKED LIKE IT WAS BUYING
 *
 * /api/us/song was the ONLY endpoint in the wing that demanded the admin token.
 * Photos, letters, the daily question, the list, the marks and her songs all
 * accepted a plain session — so anybody through the gate could already write
 * nine-tenths of the site. A second credential guarding one form out of ten is an
 * inconsistency, not a threat model, and it cost a second login on every device.
 *
 * The gate is the security boundary. Inside it there are two people who do not need
 * protecting from each other, so identity is now DECLARED rather than proved — see
 * src/pages/api/us/whoami.ts, and the switch in the hub footer.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * A REDIRECT RATHER THAN A DELETED FILE
 *
 * The path may be bookmarked or installed, and a 404 inside a standalone app is a
 * dead end with no URL bar to correct. 301 rather than 302, because this move is
 * permanent. Nothing here reads a cookie, so it redirects for either of them and
 * the destination does its own guarding.
 *
 * /api/us/admin still exists and still works. It is no longer reachable from any
 * page and nothing requires it; it is kept only so a session can be recovered from
 * a passcode if the gate answers are ever forgotten. If that is not wanted, delete
 * the route and US_ADMIN_PASSCODE_DIGEST with it.
 */
export const prerender = false;
return Astro.redirect('/samdrea/vault/today', 301);
---
